-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Concentrations and uptake of neutral monosaccharides along 140&#x000b0;W in the equatorial Pacific: contribution of glucose to heterotrophic bacterial activity and the DOM flux.</article-title><source>Limnology and Oceanography</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>604</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003416-Azam1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Azam</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodson</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1977</year><article-title>Size distribution and activity of marine microheterotrophs.</article-title><source>Limnology and Oceanography</source><volume>22</volume><fpage>492</fpage><lpage>501</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003416-Vaccaro1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vaccaro</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Hicks</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Jannasch</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Carey</surname><given-names>FG</given-names></name></person-group><year>1968</year><article-title>Occurrence and Role of Glucose in Seawater.</article-title><source>Limnology and Oceanography</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>356</fpage><lpage>360</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003416-Azam2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Azam</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodson</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1981</year><article-title>Multiphasic kinetics for D-glucose uptake by assemblages of natural marine-bacteria.</article-title><source>Marine Ecology-Progress Series</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>222</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="po